  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vijay Kumar And Another vs State Of U.P. on 28 May, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ? In Chamber Case :- Criminal Misc Anticipatory Bail Application U/S 438 Cr.P.C. No. - 2644 of 2020 Applicant :- Vijay Kumar And Another Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Shad Khan,Ajad Singh Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J.",
    "facts": "The instant Anticipatory Bail Application has been filed with a prayer to grant an anticipatory bail to the applicants, namely, Vijay Kumar and Indrajeet, in Case Crime No. 159 of 2020, under Sections 60(1)(D) Excise Act and section 272 IPC , Police Station - Rohania, District - Varanasi. Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, I.P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section 60 (1) (D) of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged Without Vijay Kumar And Another vs State Of U.P. on 28 May, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/105309362/",
    "arguments": "1 expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusation and his antecedents, the applicant is entitled to be released on anticipatory bail in this case for the limited period considering the exception considered by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal Vs. State (NCT of Delhi)-2020 SCC Online SC 98.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "1 expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusation and his antecedents, the applicant is entitled to be released on anticipatory bail in this case for the limited period considering the exception considered by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal Vs. State (NCT of Delhi)-2020 SCC Online SC 98."
